"[{\"i\":1,\"inputId\":\":r2:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 1\\nWeightage: 2\\nStatus: Evaluating\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named sqldb-ai-prod that stores customer support tickets for a multitenant software as a service (SaaS) application. sqldb-ai-prod contains a table named Tickets. Tickets contains columns named TenantId, TicketId, CustomerEmail, CustomerPhone, and Notes. You plan to harden data access, since a new support team will use ad hoc reporting tools that connect directly to sqldb-ai-prod. You need to configure security to meet the following requirements:\\nSupport agents must see only the rows of their own TenantId column.\\nSupport agents must see only the domain name portion of the CustomerEmail column.\\nInstructions: What should you do for each requirement?\\nTo answer, drag the appropriate actions to the correct requirements.\\nEach action may be used once, more than once, or not at all.\\nYou may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.\\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.\\nConfigure dynamic data masking on selected columns.\\nEnable Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) and customer-managed keys.\\nCreate a row-level security (RLS) predicate that uses the user context.\\nEncrypt sensitive columns by using Always Encrypted with Azure Key Vault.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":2,\"inputId\":\":r3:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 2\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that contains a table named Customer. Customer contains the following columns:\\nNationalIDNumber is unique per customer.\\nInvestigationNotes contains free-form text.\\nYou have a stored procedure that performs point lookups by NationalIDNumber and returns InvestigationNotes in the query results without filtering on InvestigationNotes.\\nYou need to encrypt both columns by using Always Encrypted and the highest security possible.\\nQuestion: Which type of Always Encrypted encryption should you use for each column?\\nrandomized for NationalIDNumber and randomized for InvestigationNotes\\ndeterministic for NationalIDNumber and randomized for InvestigationNotes\\ndeterministic for NationalIDNumber and deterministic for InvestigationNotes\\nrandomized for NationalIDNumber and deterministic for InvestigationNotes\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":3,\"inputId\":\":r4:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 3\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named SalesDB and an Azure App Service app named sales-api. SalesDB contains a table named dbo.Customers. dbo.Customers contains two columns named CreditCardNumber and TenantId. Currently, sales-api connects to SalesDB by using SQL authentication with a stored username and password. You need to recommend a solution that meets the following requirements:\\nProvides a passwordless method for sales-api to access SalesDB\\nEnsures that credit card numbers are NOT stored as plain text Question: What should you include in the recommendation?\\nAzure Key Vault and Always Encrypted\\nmanaged identities and dynamic data masking\\nmanaged identities and Always Encrypted\\nTransparent Data Encryption (TDE) and row-level security (RLS)\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":4,\"inputId\":\":r5:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 4\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL Database database named SalesDB that supports an AI-driven product search API.\\nAfter a new deployment, users report that API response times increased significantly.\\nYou suspect that one or more queries are taking longer to execute than before.\\nYou need to identify the long-running queries causing the increased latency.\\nWhich tool should you use?\\nAzure Monitor\\nLog Analytics\\nQuery Performance Insight\\nThe Query Store plan store\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":5,\"inputId\":\":r6:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 5\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL Database database named SalesDB with Query Store enabled.\\nUsers report that API latency increased immediately after a deployment.\\nYou suspect that a query execution plan regression occurred.\\nYou need to verify whether the affected query used different execution plans over time.\\nWhich feature should you use?\\nThe Regressed Queries pane in Query Store\\nThe Query Store plan store\\nAzure Monitor\\nLog Analytics\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":6,\"inputId\":\":r7:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 6\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have confirmed that a query execution plan regression caused increased latency in the AI-driven product search API hosted on SalesDB.\\nYou need to restore the previously efficient execution plan without making any changes to the application code.\\nWhat should you do?\\nConfigure Azure Monitor alerts\\nClear the Query Store cache\\nUse plan forcing in Query Store\\nRestart the database instance\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":7,\"inputId\":\":r8:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 7\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You manage an Azure SQL Database database named SalesDB with Query Store enabled.\\nFollowing a deployment, users report inconsistent API performance.\\nYou need to identify queries whose performance regressed compared to their historical execution statistics.\\nWhich Query Store feature should you use?\\nThe Regressed Queries pane in Query Store\\nAzure Monitor metrics\\nQuery Performance Insight\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":8,\"inputId\":\":r9:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 8\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named ProductsDB. You deploy Data API builder (DAB) to Azure Container Apps. You discover that the container app cannot connect to ProductsDB. Your development team reports that the container app is unreachable from the internet for integration tests. You need to update Azure SQL Database and Container Apps to meet the following requirements:\\nEnsure that the Azure SQL logical server allows connections from Azure services.\\nEnsure that the Container Apps environment accepts inbound requests from the public internet.\\nWhat should you configure?\\nWhat should you configure for the Azure SQL firewall rule?\\n0.0.0.0 to 0.0.0.0\\n127.0.0.1 to 127.0.0.1\\n10.0.0.0 to 10.255.255.255\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":9,\"inputId\":\":ra:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 9\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named ProductsDB. You deploy Data API builder (DAB) to Azure Container Apps. You discover that the container app cannot connect to ProductsDB. Your development team reports that the container app is unreachable from the internet for integration tests. You need to update Azure SQL Database and Container Apps to meet the following requirements:\\nEnsure that the Azure SQL logical server allows connections from Azure services.\\nEnsure that the Container Apps environment accepts inbound requests from the public internet.\\nWhat should you configure?\\nWhat should you configure for Container Apps ingress?\\nRestrict ingress to internal traffic only\\nSet ingress to external and target port 5000\\nSet ingress to internal and target port 5000\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":10,\"inputId\":\":rb:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 10\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named ToDo that contains a table named dbo.ToDo.\\nYour company plans to develop an Azure Functions app to run whenever the rows in dbo.ToDo change.\\nThe app will process INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE events by using the Azure SQL trigger binding.\\nYou need to configure ToDo to support the planned app.\\nWhat should you do?\\nOn dbo.ToDo, create a Data Definition Language (DDL) trigger that calls the Azure Functions HTTP endpoint\\nEnable change tracking on ToDo and dbo.ToDo\\nEnable change data capture (CDC) on ToDo and dbo.ToDo\\nOn dbo.ToDo, create a Data Manipulation Language (DML) trigger that calls the Azure Functions HTTP endpoint\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":11,\"inputId\":\":rc:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 11\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have a database that contains production data.\\nThe schema is stored in a Git repository as an SDK-style SQL database project and contains the following reference data.\\nName\\tData type\\nRuleId\\tint identity\\nCode\\tnvarchar(10)\\nCreateDate\\tdatetime2\\nDescription\\tnvarchar(256)\\nA deployment pipeline can be rerun automatically when a transient failure occurs.\\nYou need to deploy the reference data as part of the same CI/CD process.\\nRerunning the pipeline must produce the same outcome and must NOT create duplicate rows.\\nWhat should you do?\\nRestore a backup after each deployment.\\nStore the reference values in GitHub repository secrets\\nAdd a post-deployment script that inserts reference rows by using IF NOT EXISTS or MERGE logic.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":12,\"inputId\":\":rd:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 12\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have a GitHub Actions workflow that builds and deploys an Azure SQL database.\\nThe schema is stored in a GitHub repository as an SDK-style SQL database project.\\nFollowing a code review, you discover that you need to generate a report that shows whether the production schema has diverged from the model in source control.\\nWhich action should you add to the pipeline?\\nSqlPackage.exe /Action:DriftReport\\nSqlPackage.exe /Action:DeployReport\\nSqlPackage.exe /Action:Script\\nSqlPackage.exe /Action:Extract\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":13,\"inputId\":\":re:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 13\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure container app named app1-contoso-001 that hosts a Data API builder (DAB) container in front of an Azure SQL database.\\nYou add an entity named Todo that uses a source named dbo.todos.\\nWhich URL pattern should clients use to access the Todo REST endpoint?\\nhttps://app1-contoso-001.azurestaticapps.net/data-api/api/Todo\\nhttps://app1-contoso-001.azurestaticapps.net/api/Todo\\nhttps://app1-contoso-001.azurestaticapps.net/data-api/graphql/Todo\\nhttps://app1-contoso-001.azurestaticapps.net/data-api/Todo\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":14,\"inputId\":\":rf:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 14\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL Database database that contains a table named Sales.Customer.\\nThe Sales.Customer table contains the following columns: CustomerId FullName Email TaxID RegionId You also have a database role named AppSupport that is used by a support application.\\nYou need to implement a security solution for AppSupport that meets the following requirements: Prevent AppSupport from viewing the TaxID column.\\nAllow AppSupport to query the Sales.Customer table for troubleshooting.\\nAllow AppSupport to run a stored procedure named Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId.\\nWhich Transact-SQL statements should you use?\\nYou need to allow AppSupport to execute the stored procedure named Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId.\\nWhich statement should you use?\\nGRANT SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId TO AppSupport;\\nGRANT EXECUTE ON OBJECT::Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId TO AppSupport;\\nDENY EXECUTE ON OBJECT::Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId TO AppSupport;\\nREVOKE EXECUTE ON OBJECT::Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId FROM AppSupport;\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":15,\"inputId\":\":rg:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 15\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL Database database that contains a table named Sales.Customer.\\nThe Sales.Customer table contains the following columns: CustomerId FullName Email TaxID RegionId You also have a database role named AppSupport that is used by a support application.\\nYou need to implement a security solution for AppSupport that meets the following requirements: Prevent AppSupport from viewing the TaxID column.\\nAllow AppSupport to query the Sales.Customer table for troubleshooting.\\nAllow AppSupport to run a stored procedure named Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId.\\nYou need to prevent AppSupport from viewing the TaxID column while still allowing access to the remaining columns in the table.\\nWhich Transact-SQL statement should you use?\\nDENY SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer TO AppSupport;\\nREVOKE SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer(TaxID) FROM AppSupport;\\nDENY SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer(TaxID) TO AppSupport;\\nGRANT SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer(TaxID) TO AppSupport;\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":16,\"inputId\":\":rh:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 16\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL Database database that contains a table named Sales.Customer.\\nThe Sales.Customer table contains the following columns: CustomerId FullName Email TaxID RegionId You also have a database role named AppSupport that is used by a support application.\\nYou need to implement a security solution for AppSupport that meets the following requirements: Prevent AppSupport from viewing the TaxID column.\\nAllow AppSupport to query the Sales.Customer table for troubleshooting.\\nAllow AppSupport to run a stored procedure named Sales.usp_GetCustomerByCustomerId.\\nYou need to allow AppSupport to query the Sales.Customer table.\\nWhich Transact-SQL statement should you use?\\nGRANT SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer TO AppSupport;\\nDENY SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer TO AppSupport;\\nGRANT EXECUTE ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer TO AppSupport;\\nREVOKE SELECT ON OBJECT::Sales.Customer FROM AppSupport;\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":17,\"inputId\":\":ri:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 17\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an SDK-style SQL database project named MyDatabaseProject.sqlproj stored in a private GitHub repository.\\nThe repository contains the following GitHub Actions workflow: The repository contains the AZURE_SQL_CONNECTION_STRING secrets.\\nThe target is an Azure SQL database that allows access to Azure services and is configured to support mixed authentication.\\nThe workflow runs successfully.\\nWhich of the statement is true?\\nThe workflow relies on a Microsoft Entra workload identity to access the target Azure SQL database.\\nChanging the Build SQL project step to run: dotnet build MyDatabaseProject.sqlproj -c Release will result in a successful deployment.\\nThe workflow can be triggered manually, without making changes to the repository.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":18,\"inputId\":\":rj:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 18\\nWeightage: 2\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric that uses the default settings for a newly created database and contains a table named Sales.Orders. You have an application that uses two stored procedures to access Sales.Orders. While monitoring database activity, you discover the following:\\nsys.dm_exec_requests shows multiple sessions in a suspended state with wait_type = LCK_M_X.\\nAll the sessions show the same wait_resource, which maps to Sales.Orders, and the same nonzero blocking_session_id.\\nsys.dm_exec_input_buffer(blocking_session_id, NULL) returns a last submitted command of BEGIN TRANSACTION UPDATE Sales.Orders.\\nsys.dm_exec_sessions for the blocking session shows status = sleeping and open_transaction_count = 1.\\nWhich of the statement is true?\\nThe blocking is caused by an uncommitted explicit transaction in the blocking session that is holding locks.\\nWhile an UPDATE operation on Sales.Orders is occurring, SELECT statements will be blocked.\\nJoining sys.dm_tran_locks to sys.dm_exec_requests will show which session holds locks involved in the blocking chain.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":19,\"inputId\":\":rk:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 19\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named ProductsDB. You deploy Data API builder (DAB) to Azure Container Apps by using the mcr.microsoft.com/azure-databases/data-api-builder:latest image. The container app has the following configurations:\\nSecrets: mssql-connection-string, dab-config-base64\\nEnvironment variables: o MSSQL_CONNECTION_STRING=secretref:mssql-connection-string o DAB_CONFIG_BASE64=secretref:dab-config-base64\\nIngress: External on port 5000 Users report that the /health endpoint returns a healthy response, but all requests that query an entity named Products fail and generate a connection error.\\nYou confirm that the SQL login in the connection string is correct and the database exists.\\nYou need to ensure that the container app can establish connections to the Azure SQL logical server without changing the container app deployment settings or the DAB configuration file.\\nTask: What should you do on the Azure SQL logical server?\\nCreate an auto-failover group for ProductsDB\\nEnable FORCE_LAST_GOOD_PLAN automatic tuning for ProductsDB\\nCreate a firewall rule that allows a start and end IP address of 0.0.0.0\\nRun DBCC CHECKDB on ProductsDB.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":20,\"inputId\":\":rl:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 20\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure AI Search service and an index named hotels that includes a vector field named DescriptionVector.\\nYou query the hotels index by using the Search Documents REST API.\\nYou need to implement a hybrid search query that uses DescriptionVector and includes semantic capabilities with captions.\\nYou need to configure the request body to enable semantic ranking for the query.\\nWhich value should you use for queryType?\\nsimple\\nsemantic\\nhybrid\\nfull\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":21,\"inputId\":\":rm:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 21\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure AI Search service and an index named hotels that includes a vector field named DescriptionVector.\\nYou query the hotels index by using the Search Documents REST API.\\nYou need to implement a hybrid search query that uses DescriptionVector and includes semantic capabilities with captions.\\nYou need to configure the semantic configuration used by the query.\\nWhich value should you use for semanticConfiguration?\\ndefault\\nsemantic\\ngenerative\\nhotels\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":22,\"inputId\":\":rn:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 22\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure AI Search service and an index named hotels that includes a vector field named DescriptionVector.\\nYou query the hotels index by using the Search Documents REST API.\\nYou need to implement a hybrid search query that uses DescriptionVector and includes captions in the response.\\nYou need to configure the captions mode in the REST request body.\\nWhich value should you use for captions?\\nnone\\ngenerative\\nextractive\\nsimple\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":23,\"inputId\":\":ro:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 23\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database that contains a table named dbo.Products.\\ndbo.Products contains three columns named Embedding, Category, and Price.\\nThe Embedding column is defined as VECTOR(1536).\\nYou use AI_GENERATE_EMBEDDINGS and VECTOR_SEARCH to support semantic search and apply additional filters on two columns named Category and Price.\\nYou plan to change the embedding model from text-embedding-ada-002 to text-embedding-3-small.\\nExisting rows already contain embeddings in the Embedding column.\\nYou need to implement the model change.\\nApplications must be able to use VECTOR_SEARCH without runtime errors.\\nWhat should you do first?\\nConvert the Embedding column to nvarchar(max).\\nCreate a vector index on dbo.Products.Embedding.\\nNormalize the vector lengths before storing new embeddings.\\nRegenerate embeddings for the existing rows.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":24,\"inputId\":\":rp:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 24\\nWeightage: 2\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a Microsoft SQL Server 2025 instance that contains a database named SalesDB.\\nSalesDB supports a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) pattern for internal support tickets.\\nThe SQL Server instance runs without any outbound network connectivity.\\nYou plan to generate embeddings inside the SQL Server instance and store them in a table for vector similarity queries.\\nYou need to ensure that only a database user account named AIApplicationUser can run embedding generation by using the model.\\nWhich two actions should you perform?\\nGrant the CONTROL permission on SalesDB to AIApplicationUser.\\nCreate an external model project that points to a Microsoft Foundry REST endpoint.\\nCreate a database audit specification on SalesDB owned by AIApplicationUser.\\nGrant the EXECUTE permission on the external model project to AIApplicationUser.\\nCreate an external model project by using ONNX runtime and local paths.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":25,\"inputId\":\":rq:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 25\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a Microsoft SQL Server 2025 instance that has a managed identity enabled.\\nYou have a database that contains a table named dbo.ManualChunks.\\ndbo.ManualChunks contains product manuals.\\nA retrieval query already returns the top five matching chunks as nvarchar(max) text.\\nYou need to call an Azure OpenAI REST endpoint for chat completions.\\nThe solution must provide the highest level of security.\\nYou write the following Transact-SQL code: SQL 01 CREATE DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL AzureOpenAIHeaders 02 [What should you insert at line 02?] 03 GO 04 CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE dbo.AskManuals ...\\n10 EXEC @retval = sys.sp_invoke_external_rest_endpoint 11 @url = N'https://.openai.azure.com/openai/deployments//chat/completions?api-version=2024-05-15-preview', 12 @method = N'POST', 13 @credential = N'AzureOpenAIHeaders',\\nWITH IDENTITY = ''HTTPEndpointQueryString'', SECRET = N''{\\\"api-key\\\":\\\"\\\"}'';\\nWITH IDENTITY = ''Managed Identity'', SECRET = N''{\\\"api-key\\\":\\\"\\\"}'';\\nWITH IDENTITY = ''AzureOpenAI'', SECRET = N''{\\\"resourceId\\\":\\\"\\\"}'';\\nWITH IDENTITY = ''HTTPEndpointHeaders'', SECRET = N''{\\\"api-key\\\":\\\"\\\"}'';\\nWITH IDENTITY = ''Managed Identity'', SECRET = ''{\\\"resourceId\\\":\\\"\\\"}'';\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":26,\"inputId\":\":rr:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 26\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database that contains tables named dbo.Tickets and dbo.TicketNotes. dbo.Tickets contains support tickets and dbo.TicketNotes contains ticket notes. A retrieval query returns the top five relevant ticket notes for a user question. You plan to implement a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) pattern that meets the following requirements:\\nFormats the retrieved relational data for large language model (LLM) processing\\nSends the user question and retrieved context to an Azure OpenAI REST endpoint for chat completions\\nExtracts the response text from the LLM response Which Transact-SQL function should you use to extract the response text?\\nJSON_VALUE(@response, ''$.choices[0].message.content'')\\nJSON_MODIFY(@response, ''$.result'')\\nJSON_QUERY(@response, ''$.choices'')\\nOPENJSON(@response)\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":27,\"inputId\":\":rs:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 27\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou need to design a generative AI solution that uses a Microsoft SQL Server 2025 database named DB1 as a data source. The solution must generate responses that meet the following requirements:\\nAre grounded in the latest transactional and reference data stored in DB1\\nDo NOT require retraining or fine-tuning the language model when the data changes\\nCan include citations or references to the source data used in the response Which scenario is the best use case for implementing a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) pattern?\\nMore than one answer choice may achieve the goal.\\nSelect the BEST answer.\\ntraining a custom language model on historical database data\\ngenerating marketing slogans based on user sentiment analysis\\nanswering user questions based on company-specific knowledge\\nsummarizing free-form user input text\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":28,\"inputId\":\":rt:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 28\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a Microsoft SQL Server 2025 database that contains a table named products.\\nproducts contains two columns named description and embedding.\\nembedding is generated from description.\\nYou have an application named App1.\\nApp1 has a feature that uses the following query: VECTOR_DISTANCE('cosine', @query_vector, embedding) Users report that the feature is slow during peak usage times.\\nYou discover that during peak usage times, the semantic search latency increases and CPU utilization spikes.\\nYou need to reduce latency and CPU utilization related to the App1 feature.\\nWhat should you do?\\nAdd a nonclustered index on products.embedding.\\nCreate a vector index on products.embedding and change the query to use VECTOR_NORMALIZE and NORM_TYPE = ''norm1''.\\nUse CONTAINSTABLE against description only and remove the vector search.\\nCreate a vector index on products.embedding and change the query to use VECTOR_SEARCH and METRIC = ''cosine''.\\nChange embedding to VARBINARY(8000).\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":29,\"inputId\":\":ru:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 29\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\n[Snippet of code showing a stored procedure dbo.AskManuals] The code builds a JSON payload for an LLM.\\nLine 13 shows FOR JSON PATH.\\nLine 21: CONCAT(@question, CHAR(10), JSON_QUERY(@chunks)) AS [messages[1].content] What should you insert at line 22?\\nFOR XML PATH, INCLUDE_NULL_VALUES\\nFOR XML AUTO, TYPE, XMLSCHEMA,\\nFOR JSON AUTO, INCLUDE_NULL_VALUES\\nFOR JSON PATH, WITHOUT_ARRAY_WRAPPER\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":30,\"inputId\":\":rv:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 30\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database that contains tables named dbo.ProductDocs and dbo.ProductDocsEmbeddings. dbo.ProductDocs contains product documentation and the following columns:\\nDocId (int)\\nTitle (nvarchar(200))\\nBody (nvarchar(max))\\nLastModified (datetime2) The documentation is edited throughout the day. dbo.ProductDocsEmbeddings contains the following columns:\\nDocId (int)\\nChunkOrder (int)\\nChunkText (nvarchar(max))\\nEmbedding (vector(1536)) The current embedding pipeline runs once per night.\\nYou need to ensure that embeddings are updated every time the underlying documentation content changes.\\nThe solution must NOT require a nightly batch process.\\nWhat should you include in the solution?\\nchange tracking on dbo.ProductDocs\\nfixed-size chunking\\ntable triggers\\na smaller embedding model\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":31,\"inputId\":\":r10:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 31\\nWeightage: 2\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that contains a table named Tickets_Embeddings. Tickets_Embeddings contains a VECTOR(1536) column. Embeddings are generated by using text-embedding-ada-002 and the /openai/v1/embeddings endpoint. After a review of the current environment, the following changes are requested:\\nThe AI architect has recommended switching to text-embedding-3-small.\\nThe security team requires authentication by using Microsoft Entra managed identities only.\\nStoring API keys in an application is prohibited.\\nQuestion: Which two actions should you include in the solution?\\nEach correct answer presents a complete solution.\\nChange the primary keys for the tickets.\\nAlter the database tables.\\nChange the endpoint.\\nRegenerate all the embeddings.\\nAdd a firewall rule.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":32,\"inputId\":\":r11:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 32\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that contains a table named Rooms.\\nRooms was created by using the following Transact-SQL statement: SQL CREATE TABLE Rooms ( RoomID int PRIMARY KEY, Owner nvarchar(100), Capacity int ); You discover that some records in the Rooms table contain NULL values for the Owner field.\\nYou need to ensure that all future records have a value for the Owner field.\\nQuestion: What should you add?\\na unique constraint\\na foreign key\\na check constraint\\na nonclustered index\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":33,\"inputId\":\":r12:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 33\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: Your team is developing an Azure SQL database solution from a locally cloned GitHub repository by using Microsoft Visual Studio Code and GitHub Copilot Chat.\\nYou need to ensure that GitHub Copilot Chat uses the team's coding standards when generating Transact-SQL code in Visual Studio Code.\\nQuestion: What should you use?\\n.github/copilot-instructions.md\\n.vscode/settings.json\\n%APPDATA%\\\\Code\\\\User\\\\copilot-instructions.md\\n%APPDATA%\\\\Code\\\\User\\\\settings.json\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":34,\"inputId\":\":r13:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 34\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: Your development team uses Microsoft Visual Studio Code with the MSSQL extension and the GitHub Copilot Chat extension.\\nThe team connects to an Azure SQL database by using individual database logins and uses the @mssql chat participant to generate and run Transact-SQL queries from prompts.\\nQuestion: What is used to ensure that GitHub Copilot Chat-generated queries run in the context of the developer?\\nshared MCP instruction files\\nSQL permissions\\nGitHub organization permissions\\nAzure role-based access control (Azure RBAC) permissions\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":35,\"inputId\":\":r14:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 35\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL managed instance that supports a gaming leaderboard API and contains a table named dbo.Leaderboard.\\nYou plan to reduce write latency during peak events of dbo.Leaderboard.\\nYou need to ensure that dbo.Leaderboard supports point lookups.\\nThe leaderboard information does NOT need to persist after a restart.\\nQuestion: Which type of table should you configure?\\nRowstore disk-based\\nSCHEMA_AND_DATA in-memory\\nSCHEMA_ONLY in-memory\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":36,\"inputId\":\":r15:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 36\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL managed instance that supports a gaming leaderboard API and contains a table named dbo.Leaderboard.\\nYou plan to reduce write latency during peak events of dbo.Leaderboard.\\nYou need to ensure that dbo.Leaderboard supports point lookups.\\nThe leaderboard information does NOT need to persist after a restart.\\nQuestion: Which type of index should you configure?\\nHASH\\nNonclustered\\nNonclustered columnstore\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":37,\"inputId\":\":r16:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 37\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: Your team is developing an Azure SQL dataset solution from a locally cloned GitHub repository by using Microsoft Visual Studio Code and GitHub Copilot Chat.\\nYou need to disable the GitHub Copilot repository-level instructions for yourself without affecting other users.\\nQuestion: What should you do?\\nDelete .github/copilot-instructions.md.\\nAdd a --debug flag when you start the GitHub Copilot Chat extension.\\nFrom Visual Studio Code, modify your GitHub Copilot Chat user settings.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":38,\"inputId\":\":r17:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 38\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that stores sales data and contains tables named Sales and Products.\\nSales contains three columns named SalesDate, ProductKey, and TotalSale.\\nSales is 10 TB and is loaded nightly by using a batch process.\\nMost reporting queries scan large portions of sales, filter on SalesDate or ProductKey, and use SUM() to aggregate TotalSale.\\nProducts is relatively small and is used primarily for point lookups and joins to Sales.\\nTask: You need to recommend which indexes to create to optimize the reporting queries.\\nThe solution must minimize storage requirements.\\nWhich type of index should you recommend for Sales table?\\nA clustered columnstore index\\nA clustered rowstore index\\nA nonclustered columnstore index\\nA nonclustered rowstore index\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":39,\"inputId\":\":r18:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 39\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that stores sales data and contains tables named Sales and Products.\\nSales contains three columns named SalesDate, ProductKey, and TotalSale.\\nSales is 10 TB and is loaded nightly by using a batch process.\\nMost reporting queries scan large portions of sales, filter on SalesDate or ProductKey, and use SUM() to aggregate TotalSale.\\nProducts is relatively small and is used primarily for point lookups and joins to Sales.\\nTask: You need to recommend which indexes to create to optimize the reporting queries.\\nThe solution must minimize storage requirements.\\nWhich type of index should you recommend for Product table?\\nA clustered columnstore index\\nA clustered rowstore index\\nA nonclustered columnstore index\\nA nonclustered rowstore index\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":40,\"inputId\":\":r19:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 40\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You are developing an Azure SQL solution by using Microsoft Visual Studio 2025.\\nThe solution uses a GitHub repository.\\nYou plan to use GitHub Copilot Chat to access the GitHub repository tools by connecting to the GitHub MCP Server.\\nYou need to configure Visual Studio to support the planned configuration.\\nThe solution must rely on OAuth to access the MCP server.\\nQuestion: What should you create?\\nthe \\\\.vscode\\\\settings.json file that contains a URL of https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/\\nthe \\\\.vs\\\\settings.json file that contains the personal access token (PAT) that has the repo scope\\nthe \\\\.mcp.json file that contains a URL of https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/\\nthe \\\\.github\\\\mcp.json file that contains the personal access token (PAT) that has the repo scope\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":41,\"inputId\":\":r1a:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 41\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a GitHub Enterprise subscription.\\nYour team is developing an Azure SQL dataset solution from a locally cloned GitHub repository by using Microsoft Visual Studio Code and GitHub Copilot Chat.\\nA mix of GitHub Copilot instructions is configured at different levels, including organization-wide, repository-wide, agent-specific, and personal.\\nWhich instructions will take precedence over the others?\\npersonal\\norganization-wide\\nrepository-wide\\nagent-specific\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":42,\"inputId\":\":r1b:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 42\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou are developing an Azure SQL database solution from a locally cloned GitHub repository by using Microsoft Visual Studio Code and GitHub Copilot Chat.\\nYou need to ensure that GitHub Copilot Chat can call the hosted GitHub MCP Server tools by using OAuth.\\nThe MCP server configuration must be scoped to the repository.\\nWhat should you do in Visual Studio Code?\\nFrom the Command Palette, enter MCP: add server, select HTTP (HTTP or Server-Sent Events), enter https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/, and then save the configuration to the user settings\\nCreate a personal access token (PAT) that has the repo scope and store the PAT in the .vscode/mcp.json file as the Authorization header.\\nFrom the Command Palette, enter MCP: add server, select HTTP (HTTP or Server-Sent Events), enter https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/, and then save the configuration to the workspace settings.\\nCreate a personal access token (PAT) that has the repo scope and store the PAT in the .github/mcp.json file as the Authorization header.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":43,\"inputId\":\":r1c:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 43\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric that contains a table named dbo.Orders.\\ndbo.Orders has a clustered index, contains three years of data, and is partitioned by a column named OrderDate by month.\\nYou need to remove all the rows for the oldest month.\\nThe solution must minimize the impact on other queries that access the data in dbo.Orders.\\nSolution: Run the following Transact-SQL statement: TRUNCATE TABLE dbo.Orders; Does this meet the goal?\\nYes\\nNo\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":44,\"inputId\":\":r1d:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 44\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric that contains a table named dbo.Orders.\\ndbo.Orders has a clustered index, contains three years of data, and is partitioned by a column named OrderDate by month.\\nYou need to remove all the rows for the oldest month.\\nThe solution must minimize the impact on other queries that access the data in dbo.Orders.\\nSolution: Run the following Transact-SQL statement: DELETE FROM dbo.Orders WHERE OrderDate < DATEADD(month, -36, SYSUTCDATETIME()); Does this meet the goal?\\nYes\\nNo\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":45,\"inputId\":\":r1e:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 45\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric that contains a table named dbo.Orders.\\ndbo.Orders has a clustered index, contains three years of data, and is partitioned by a column named OrderDate by month.\\nYou need to remove all the rows for the oldest month.\\nThe solution must minimize the impact on other queries that access the data in dbo.Orders.\\nSolution: Identify the partition number for the oldest month, and then run the following Transact-SQL statement: TRUNCATE TABLE dbo.Orders WITH (PARTITIONS (partition number)); Does this meet the goal?\\nYes\\nNo\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":46,\"inputId\":\":r1f:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 46\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an SDK-style SQL database project stored in a Git repository.\\nThe project targets an Azure SQL Database.\\nThe CI build fails with unresolved reference errors when the project references system objects.\\nYou need to update the SQL database project to ensure that dotnet build validates successfully by including the correct system objects in the database model for Azure SQL Database.\\nSolution: Build the project by running dotnet build -bl -flp:v=diag.\\nDoes this meet the goal?\\nYes\\nNo\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":47,\"inputId\":\":r1g:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 47\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an SDK-style SQL database project stored in a Git repository.\\nThe project targets an Azure SQL Database.\\nThe CI build fails with unresolved reference errors when the project references system objects.\\nYou need to update the SQL database project to ensure that dotnet build validates successfully by including the correct system objects in the database model for Azure SQL Database.\\nSolution: Add the Microsoft.SqlServer.Dacpacs.Master NuGet package to the project.\\nDoes this meet the goal?\\nYes\\nNo\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":48,\"inputId\":\":r1h:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 48\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric that contains a table named dbo.Orders.\\ndbo.Orders has a clustered index, contains three years of data, and is partitioned by a column named OrderDate by month.\\nYou need to remove all the rows for the oldest month.\\nThe solution must minimize the impact on other queries that access the data in dbo.Orders.\\nSolution: Identify the partition scheme for the oldest month, and then run the following Transact-SQL statement: ALTER TABLE dbo.Orders DROP PARTITION SCHEME (partition_scheme_name); Does this meet the goal?\\nYes\\nNo\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":49,\"inputId\":\":r1i:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 49\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named SalesDB. You have a Data API builder (DAB) instance that exposes the following entities in SalesDB:\\nA table entity named Order mapped to a table named dbo.Orders.\\nA stored procedure entity named FinalizeOrder mapped to a stored procedure named dbo.usp_FinalizeOrder.\\nThe DAB runtime configuration includes the following permissions: JSON { \\\"entities\\\": { \\\"Order\\\": { \\\"source\\\": \\\"dbo.Orders\\\", \\\"permissions\\\": [ { \\\"role\\\": \\\"authenticated\\\", \\\"actions\\\": [\\\"read\\\"] } ] }, \\\"FinalizeOrder\\\": { \\\"source\\\": \\\"dbo.usp_FinalizeOrder\\\", \\\"permissions\\\": [ { \\\"role\\\": \\\"operations\\\", \\\"actions\\\": [\\\"execute\\\"], \\\"policy\\\": { \\\"database\\\": \\\"TenantId = @claims.tenantId\\\" } } ] } } } Client requests include a Microsoft Entra access token.\\nThe client also sends HTTP header X-MS-API-ROLE: operations for both REST and GraphQL requests.\\nWhich of the following statements is true?\\nA REST GET request to the Order entity that includes the access token and X-MS-API-ROLE: operations will return data\\nWhen DAB runs the stored procedure, the database policy defined on the FinalizeOrder entity will be enforced.\\nIf the client omits the X-MS-API-ROLE header but still sends the same access token, the Order entity read...\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":50,\"inputId\":\":r1j:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 50\\nWeightage: 3\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have a database named db1.\\nThe schema is stored in a Git repository as an SDK-style SQL database project.\\nThe repository contains the following GitHub Action workflow.\\nWorkflow Snippet: YAML name: Database CI/CD on: push: branches: [ main ] pull_request: branches: [ main ] jobs: build-and-deploy: runs-on: ubuntu-latest steps: - name: Checkout code uses: actions/checkout@v3 - name: Setup .NET uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v3 with: dotnet-version: '8.x' - name: Build run: dotnet build db1.sqlproj --configuration Release - name: Deploy run: | SqlPackage /Action:Publish \\\\ /SourceFile:./bin/Release/db1.dacpac \\\\ /TargetConnectionString:\\\"${{ secrets.Target_Connection_String }}\\\" unit-tests: runs-on: ubuntu-latest needs: build-and-deploy if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' steps: - name: Checkout code uses: actions/checkout@v3 - name: Setup .NET uses: actions/setup-dotnet@v3 with: dotnet-version: '8.x' - name: Run unit tests run: dotnet test UnitTests.csproj --configuration Release Which of the following statements is true?\\nUnit tests run automatically whenever changes are pushed to main.\\nSchema validation occurs during the Build step.\\nSchema validation occurs during the Deploy step.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":51,\"inputId\":\":r1k:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 51\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that supports a customer-facing API.\\nThe API calls a stored procedure named dbo.GetCustomerOrders thousands of times per hour.\\nAfter a deployment that updated indexes and statistics, users report that the API endpoint is slower.\\nIn Query Store, the same query now has two persisted execution plans.\\nDuring the last hour, the newer plan had a significantly higher average duration and CPU time than the older plan.\\nYou need to restore the previous performance quickly, without changing the API code.\\nWhich Transact-SQL command should you run?\\nEXEC sys.sp_query_store_set_hints\\nALTER DATABASE\\nDBCC FREEPROCCACHE\\nEXEC sp_query_store_force_plan\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":52,\"inputId\":\":r1l:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 52\\nWeightage: 2\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database named AdventureWorksDB that contains a table named dbo.Employee. You have a C# Azure Functions app that uses an HTTP-triggered function with an Azure SQL input binding to query dbo.Employee. You are adding a second function that will react to row changes in dbo.Employee and write structured logs. Requirements:\\nChanges to dbo.Employee must trigger the new function within five seconds.\\nEach invocation must process no more than 100 changes.\\nWhich two database configurations should you perform?\\nEnable change data capture (CDC) for dbo.Employee table changes.\\nEnable change tracking on the dbo.Employee table.\\nCreate an AFTER trigger on dbo.Employee for Data Manipulation Language (DML).\\nSet Sql_Trigger_MaxBatchSize to 100.\\nEnable change tracking at the database level.\\nSet Sql_Trigger_PollingIntervalMs to 5000.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":53,\"inputId\":\":r1m:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 53\\nWeightage: 2\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that has Query Store enabled. Query Performance Insight shows that one stored procedure has the longest runtime. The procedure runs the following parameterized query: SQL CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE dbo.GetRecentOrders @CustomerId int, @SinceDate datetime2 AS SELECT TOP (50) o.OrderId, o.OrderDate, o.Status, o.TotalAmount FROM dbo.Orders AS o WHERE o.CustomerId = @CustomerId AND o.OrderDate >= @SinceDate ORDER BY o.OrderDate DESC; The dbo.Orders table has approximately 120 million rows. CustomerId is highly selective, and OrderDate is used for range filtering and sorting. You have the following indexes:\\nClustered index: PK_Orders ON (OrderId)\\nNonclustered index: IX_Orders_OrderDate ON (OrderDate) with no included columns An actual execution plan captured from Query Store for slow runs shows the following:\\nAn index seek on IX_Orders_OrderDate followed by a Key Lookup (Clustered) on PK_Orders for CustomerId, Status, and TotalAmount.\\nA sort operator before TOP (50), because the results are ordered by OrderDate DESC.\\nWhich of the following statements are true?\\nTo avoid the explicit sort for the query, create a nonclustered index on (CustomerId, OrderDate DESC) that includes (Status, TotalAmount)\\nTo eliminate the sort and make the query use an ordered seek, add CustomerId as an included colu…\"},{\"i\":54,\"inputId\":\":r1n:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 54\\nWeightage: 3\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a database named DB1. The schema is stored in a GitHub repository as an SDK-style SQL database project. You use a feature branch workflow to deploy changes to DB1. You need to update the local feature branch with the latest changes to main, and then create a pull request to merge the feature branch into main for review. Instruction: How should you complete the GitHub CLI script? To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct targets. Each value may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content. NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point. Values:\\ngh pr create\\ngh pr merge\\ngh pr ready\\ngit checkout main\\ngit fetch origin\\ngit merge origin/main\\ngit pull origin main Answer Area: Bash git checkout feature/db1-add-staticdata [Value] [Value] [Value] \\\\ --title \\\"Feature Update: DB1\\\" \\\\ --body \\\"Apply latest improvements and updates for review\\\" \\\\ --head feature/db1-add-staticdata \\\\ --base main \\\\ --repo /DB1 \\\\ --web\\ngit fetch origin\\ngit merge origin/main\\ngh pr create\\ngh pr ready\\ngit pull origin main\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":55,\"inputId\":\":r1o:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 55\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure subscription. The subscription contains an Azure SQL database named SalesDB and an Azure App Service app named sales-api. sales-api uses virtual network integration to a subnet named vnet-prod/subnet-app and reads from SalesDB. You need to configure authentication and network access to meet the following requirements:\\nEnsure that sales-api connects to SalesDB by using passwordless authentication.\\nEnsure that all the database traffic remains within the subscription.\\nThe solution must minimize administrative effort.\\nInstruction: What should you configure for Authentication for sales-api?\\nConfigure client certificate authentication for sales-api\\nUse a connection string with rotated SQL credentials weekly\\nEnable a managed identity and use Microsoft Entra authentication\\nCreate a SQL login and store the SQL credentials in Azure Key Vault\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":56,\"inputId\":\":r1p:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 56\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure subscription. The subscription contains an Azure SQL database named SalesDB and an Azure App Service app named sales-api. sales-api uses virtual network integration to a subnet named vnet-prod/subnet-app and reads from SalesDB. You need to configure authentication and network access to meet the following requirements:\\nEnsure that sales-api connects to SalesDB by using passwordless authentication.\\nEnsure that all the database traffic remains within the subscription.\\nThe solution must minimize administrative effort.\\nInstruction: What should you configure for Network access for SalesDB?\\nAllow Azure services and keep the public endpoint enabled\\nCreate a private endpoint and disable public network access\\nAdd IP firewall rules for the App Service outbound IP addresses\\nConfigure a database-level firewall rule for support IP addresses\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":57,\"inputId\":\":r1q:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 57\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database. You deploy Data API builder (DAB) to Azure Container Apps by using the mcr.microsoft.com/azure-databases/data-api-builder:latest image. You have the following Container Apps secrets:\\nMSSQL_CONNECTION_STRING that maps to the SQL connection string\\nDAB_CONFIG_BASE64 that maps to the DAB configuration You need to initialize the DAB configuration to read the SQL connection string.\\nInstruction: Which command should you run?\\ndab init --database-type mssql --connection-string \\\"@env(''DAB_CONFIG_BASE64'')\\\" --host-mode Production --config dab-config.json\\ndab init --database-type mssql --connection-string \\\"secretref:mssql-connection-string\\\" --host-mode Production --config dab-config.json\\ndab init --database-type mssql --connection-string \\\"@env(''MSSQL_CONNECTION_STRING'')\\\" --host-mode Production --config dab-config.json\\ndab init --database-type mssql --connection-string \\\"secretref:DAB_CONFIG_BASE64\\\" --host-mode Production --config dab-config.json\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":58,\"inputId\":\":r1r:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 58\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a database named DB1.\\nThe schema is stored in a Git repository as an SDK-style SQL database project.\\nYou have a GitHub Actions workflow that already runs dotnet build and produces a database artifact.\\nYou need to add a deployment step that publishes the .dacpac file to an Azure SQL database by using the secrets stored in GitHub repository secrets.\\nInstruction: What should you include in the workflow?\\nyaml name: Publish run: | dotnet build db1.sqlproj /p:TargetConnectionString=\\\"${{ secrets.SQL_CONNECTION_STRING }}\\\"\\nyaml name: Publish uses: azure/sql-action@v2 with: action: extract path: bin/Debug/db1.dacpac connection-string: ${{ secrets.SQL_CONNECTION_STRING }}\\nyaml name: Publish uses: azure/sql-action@v2 with: action: publish path: bin/Debug/db1.dacpac connection-string: ${{ secrets.SQL_CONNECTION_STRING }}\\nyaml env: SQL_CONNECTION_STRING: Server=tcp:myserver.database.windows.net; ... steps: name: Publish uses: azure/sql-action@v2 with: action: publish path: bin/Debug/db1.dacpac connection-string: ${{ env.SQL_CONNECTION_STRING }}\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":59,\"inputId\":\":r1s:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 59\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a Microsoft Fabric workspace named Workspace1 that contains a SQL database named SalesDB and an API for GraphQL item named SalesApi. You have a Microsoft Entra group named SqlUsers. From Workspace1, you assign permission to SalesApi as shown in the following exhibit:\\nGroup: SqlUsers\\nAdditional permissions: [Checked] View and Edit GraphQL item\\nNotification Options: [Checked] Notify recipients by email The connection to SalesDB has the connectivity option configured as shown in the following exhibit:\\n[Selected] Connect to Fabric data sources with single sign-on (SSO) authentication SqlUsers has the Viewer role for Workspace1.\\nWhich of the following statements is true?\\nThe members of SqlUsers can modify the data in SalesDB via SalesApi.\\nThe members of SqlUsers can view the data in SalesDB via SalesApi.\\nThe members of SqlUsers can change the field mappings of SalesApi.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":60,\"inputId\":\":r1t:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 60\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database named SalesDB on a logical server named sales-sql01.\\nYou have an Azure App Service web app named OrderApi that connects to SalesDB by using SQL authentication.\\nYou enable a user-assigned managed identity named OrderApi-Id for OrderApi.\\nYou need to configure OrderApi to connect to SalesDB by using Microsoft Entra authentication.\\nThe managed identity must have read and write permissions to SalesDB.\\nWhich Transact-SQL statements should you run in SalesDB?\\nCREATE LOGIN [OrderApi-Id] FROM EXTERNAL PROVIDER; ALTER ROLE db_datareader ADD MEMBER [OrderApi-Id]; ALTER ROLE db_datawriter ADD MEMBER [OrderApi-Id];\\nCREATE LOGIN [OrderApi-Id] WITH PASSWORD = ''P@ssw0rd!''; ALTER SERVER ROLE sysadmin ADD MEMBER [OrderApi-Id];\\nCREATE USER [OrderApi-Id] WITH PASSWORD = ''P@ssw0rd!''; ALTER ROLE db_datareader ADD MEMBER [OrderApi-Id]; ALTER ROLE db_datawriter ADD MEMBER [OrderApi-Id];\\nCREATE USER [OrderApi-Id] FROM EXTERNAL PROVIDER; ALTER ROLE db_datareader ADD MEMBER [OrderApi-Id]; ALTER ROLE db_datawriter ADD MEMBER [OrderApi-Id];\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":61,\"inputId\":\":r1u:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 61\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database that supports the OLTP workload of an order-processing application. During a 10-minute incident window, you run a dynamic management view query and discover the following:\\nSession 72 is sleeping with open_transaction_count = 1.\\nMultiple other sessions show blocking_session_id = 72 in sys.dm_exec_requests.\\nsys.dm_exec_input_buffer(72, NULL) returns only BEGIN TRANSACTION UPDATE Sales.Orders.\\nUsers report that updates to Sales.Orders intermittently time out during the incident window.\\nThe timeouts stop only after you manually terminate session 72.\\nWhat is a possible cause of the blocking?\\nA lock escalation occurred.\\nA long-running SELECT statement is blocking writers.\\nSession 72 caused a deadlock.\\nAn explicit transaction was started but not committed or rolled back.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":62,\"inputId\":\":r1v:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 62\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database that contains a column named Notes.\\nA security review discovers that Notes contains sensitive data.\\nYou need to ensure that the data is protected so that neither the stored values nor the query inputs reveal information about the actual data.\\nThe solution must prevent a user from inferring relationships or repetitions in the data based on the encrypted output.\\nWhich should you use?\\nAlways Encrypted with secure enclaves\\nAlways Encrypted with randomized encryption\\nAlways Encrypted with deterministic encryption\\nrow-level security (RLS)\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":63,\"inputId\":\":r20:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 63\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database that contains the following SQL graph tables:\\nA NODE table named dbo.Person\\nAn EDGE table named dbo.Knows Each row in dbo.Person contains the following columns:\\nPersonId (int)\\nDisplayName (nvarchar(100)) You need to use a MATCH operator and exactly two directed Knows relationships to return the PersonId and DisplayName of people that are reachable from the person identified by an input parameter named @StartPersonId.\\nWhich Transact-SQL query should you use?\\nSELECT p3.PersonId, p3.DisplayName FROM dbo.Person AS p1 JOIN dbo.Knows AS k1 ON 1 = 1 JOIN dbo.Person AS p2 ON 1 = 1 JOIN dbo.Knows AS k2 ON 1 = 1 JOIN dbo.Person AS p3 ON 1 = 1 WHERE p1.PersonId = @StartPersonId AND MATCH(p3<-(k2)-p2<-(k1)-p1);\\nSELECT p3.PersonId, p3.DisplayName FROM dbo.Person AS p1, dbo.Knows AS k1, dbo.Person AS p2, dbo.Knows AS k2, dbo.Person AS p3 WHERE p1.PersonId = @StartPersonId AND MATCH(p1-(k1)->p2) AND MATCH(p2-(k2)- >p3);\\nSELECT p3.PersonId, p3.DisplayName FROM dbo.Person AS p1, dbo.Knows AS k1, dbo.Person AS p2, dbo.Knows AS k2, dbo.Person AS p3 WHERE p1.PersonId = @StartPersonId AND MATCH(p1-(k1)->p2-(k2)->p3);\\nSELECT p2.PersonId, @StartPersonId FROM dbo.Person AS p1, dbo.Knows AS k1, dbo.Person AS p2, dbo.Knows AS k2, dbo.Person AS p3 WHERE p1.DisplayName = p2.DisplayName AND MATCH(p1-(k1)->p2-(k2)->p3);\\nYou…\"},{\"i\":64,\"inputId\":\":r21:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 64\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL database that stores order data.\\nA reporting query aggregates monthly revenue per customer runs frequently.\\nYou need to reduce how long it takes to retrieve the calculated values.\\nThe solution must NOT alter any underlying table structure.\\nWhat should you do?\\nCreate a view by using ORDER BY without TOP, and then create a unique clustered index on the view.\\nCreate a view by using GROUP BY, and then create a unique clustered index on the view.\\nCreate a view without using WITH SCHEMABINDING, and then create a nonclustered index on the view.\\nCreate a view by using WITH SCHEMABINDING, include COUNT_BIG(*), and then create a unique clustered index on the view.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":65,\"inputId\":\":r22:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 65\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have a GitHub Codespaces environment that has GitHub Copilot Chat installed and is connected to a SQL database in Microsoft Fabric named DB1.\\nDB1 contains tables named Sales.Orders and Sales.Customers.\\nYou use GitHub Copilot Chat in the context of DB1.\\nA company policy prohibits sharing customer Personally Identifiable Information (PII), secrets, and query result sets with any AI service.\\nYou need to use GitHub Copilot Chat to write and review Transact-SQL code for a new stored procedure that will join Sales.Orders to Sales.Customers and return customer names and email addresses.\\nThe solution must NOT share the actual data in the tables with GitHub Copilot Chat.\\nWhat should you do?\\nRun a SELECT statement that returns customer names and email addresses and provide the result set to GitHub Copilot Chat so that GitHub Copilot Chat can generate the stored procedure.\\nFrom Sales.Customers, paste several rows that include email addresses into a chat, so that GitHub Copilot Chat can infer edge cases.\\nAsk GitHub Copilot Chat to generate the stored procedure by using schema details only.\\nProvide the database connection string to GitHub Copilot Chat so that GitHub Copilot Chat can validate the stored procedure.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":66,\"inputId\":\":r23:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 66\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYour development team uses GitHub Copilot Chat in Microsoft SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS) to generate and run Transact-SQL queries against an Azure SQL database named DB1.\\nDB1 contains tables that store sensitive customer data.\\nYou need to ensure that any Transact-SQL queries that run from GitHub Copilot Chat in SSMS are restricted by the same permissions as the developer's database login.\\nWhat prevents the GitHub Copilot Chat-run queries from accessing data beyond the developer's access?\\nGitHub Copilot Chat filters query results on the client side to remove rows the developer is unauthorized to see.\\nGitHub Copilot Chat runs queries in a read-only sandbox that is isolated from production database permissions.\\nGitHub Copilot Chat uses different row-level security (RLS) policies than the developer.\\nGitHub Copilot Chat runs queries by using the developer''s database identity and permissions.\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":67,\"inputId\":\":r24:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 67\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nScenario: You have an Azure SQL database that supports an AI-enabled product catalog API.\\nThe database contains a table named Sales.Orders.\\nSales.Orders contains 20 million rows and has a nonclustered index on a column named CreateDate.\\nThe API passes a date parameter named @OrderDate.\\nYou have a stored procedure named get_latest_day_orders that filters by running the following query: WHERE CAST(CreateDate AS date) = @OrderDate A review of the query execution reveals that the query causes an index scan.\\nYou need to modify the predicate to ensure that Microsoft SQL Server can use an index seek on CreateDate for a single day.\\nQuestion: Which WHERE clause should you use?\\nWHERE CONVERT(char(10), CreateDate, 121) = CONVERT(char(10), @OrderDate, 121)\\nWHERE LEFT(CONVERT(varchar(30), CreateDate, 121), 10) = CONVERT(char(10), @OrderDate, 121)\\nWHERE CreateDate >= @OrderDate AND CreateDate < DATEADD(day, 1, @OrderDate)\\nWHERE CreateDate LIKE CONVERT(char(10), @OrderDate, 121) + ''%''\\nYour Submission\"},{\"i\":68,\"inputId\":\":r25:\",\"name\":null,\"placeholder\":null,\"readOnly\":false,\"hasValue\":false,\"text\":\"Problem Statement 68\\nWeightage: 1\\nStatus: Unattempted\\nYou have an Azure SQL table that contains the following data.\\nFaqId\\tProductName\\tQuestion\\tAnswer\\n1\\tLaptop Pro\\tDoes it support USB-C charging?\\tYes, it supports USB-C charging.\\n2\\tTablet X\\tDoes it support a stylus?\\tIt supports the Active Pen stylus.\\nYou need to retrieve data to be used as context for a large language model (LLM).\\nThe solution must minimize token usage.\\nWhich format should you use to send the data to the LLM?\\nJSON [ { \\\"ProductName\\\": \\\"Laptop Pro\\\", \\\"Question\\\": \\\"Does it support USB-C charging?\\\", \\\"Answer\\\": \\\"Yes, it supports USB-C charging.\\\" }, { \\\"ProductName\\\": \\\"Tablet X\\\", \\\"Question\\\": \\\"Does it support a stylus?\\\", \\\"Answer\\\": \\\"It supports the Active Pen stylus.\\\" } ]\\nJSON [ { \\\"FaqId\\\": 1, \\\"ProductName\\\": \\\"Laptop Pro\\\", \\\"Question\\\": \\\"Does it support USB-C charging?\\\", \\\"Answer\\\": \\\"Yes, it supports USB-C charging.\\\" }, { \\\"FaqId\\\": 2, \\\"ProductName\\\": \\\"Tablet X\\\", \\\"Question\\\": \\\"Does it support a stylus?\\\", \\\"Answer\\\": \\\"It supports the Active Pen stylus.\\\" } ]\\nJSON [ { \\\"Prompt\\\": \\\"Yes, it supports USB-C charging.\\\" }, { \\\"Prompt\\\": \\\"It supports the Active Pen stylus.\\\" } ]\\nJSON [ { \\\"FaqId\\\": 1, \\\"Question\\\": \\\"Does it support USB-C charging?\\\", \\\"Answer\\\": \\\"Yes, it supports USB-C charging.\\\" }, { \\\"FaqId\\\": 2, \\\"Question\\\": \\\"Does it support a stylus?\\\", \\\"Answer\\\": \\\"It supports the Active Pen stylus.\\\" } ]\\nYour Submission\"}]"